id=a52sxq_lockstar_aod_prewarm
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: no LockStar cold start on SystemUI's main thread when the screen goes off
author=kusti420
description=UNTESTED-ON-DEVICE. Each AOD session creates AODService's PluginAODImpl inside SystemUI, and its BrightnessManager reads the AOD brightness from Good Lock LockStar's LockEditorDataProvider synchronously on SystemUI's main thread. LockStar is an empty cached process that ActivityManager kills 30-60 s after use, so going from an unlocked phone to AOD usually cold-starts it while the main thread waits: 9.3.48 log 2026-10-17, 540 ms (10:24:51) and 258 ms (10:23:32) with the home screen frozen (1029 ms Davey frame), DOZE INITIALIZED 0.8 s after goToSleep. LockStar's provider is now acquired and released at once from a background thread when the side key goes down on a lit screen (system_server, PhoneWindowManager.interceptPowerKeyDown, ~300 ms before goToSleep) and when SystemUI is told the screen is going to sleep (KeyguardService onStartedGoingToSleep, covers timeout and double tap), so the process is already up when the AOD plugin asks. Only with aod_mode != 0; without LockStar installed it is one failed lookup. logcat tag K4LockStarPrewarm logs how long the start took.
